WEBVTT

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.940
This uncivilized sound...

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.720
What are you doing?

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:27.750
Huh? Um...

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.520
The compressor

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.300
makes a nice sound, doesn't it?

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.820
Whoa! You get it, too?

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.900
I know someone named Morita who's into trains.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.400
Oh, are you...

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.430
<i>Search complete!</i>

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.810
<b>Peace Party 

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:43.810
Oh!

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.120
I thought so! You're Naganuma-san!

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:47.560
Huh?

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.590
Good luck in the gubernatorial elections!

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.190
You take your work seriously. I like that!

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.320
Thank you! I'll do my best.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.950
I'll be cheering you on!

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.740
<b>From: Chief Yamabuki 
To: Hoshimiya Haruka 

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:57.740
Thank you.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.320
Huh?

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.970
I'll do my best to represent 
the voices of the people.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.930
I was looking forward to an 
abandoned train-line tour...

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.490
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:20.010
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:26.020
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.760
<b>File 7: Long Rail Life</b>

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.930
<b>Terao Kazuyoshi Office</b>

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.050
Perp is currently heading west 
from Governor Terao's office,

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.200
on Shin Mejiro Avenue!

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.030
The governor was out of the office, 
and no property damage was done!

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.400
Stop right there!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:01.990
Stop!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.740
What's with that Willwear?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:09.330
Retreat!

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.500
Retreat!

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.920
<b>Target</b>

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.720
Seriously?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.050
We'll handle luring the perp, 
so please take care of him!

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.260
That's what we'd like to do, but...

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.810
Do we have the prefecture's go-ahead yet?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.930
There's zero chance of that.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.600
I'm getting a BS reason about how the 
prefecture's roads can't be destroyed.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.060
God!

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.200
Sorry to be late!

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.630
Sorry, and on your day off, too.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:44.660
No problem.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.080
Wow, this looks a pain in the butt.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.690
Target is currently en route toward the 
metropolitan government building at 2kph.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:57.000
It appears the EM dome uses parts from 
an overseas arms manufacturer.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.960
What's he after?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.770
Punishing the governor.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.720
Huh?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.260
<b>If nothing changes in the government,
Tokyo is finished.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.150
There was a post on a social 
network site about the attack.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.010
<b>Governor, become the victim of a lightning strike. 
Today is the day you'll be judged. 

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.490
<b>I will neither run nor hide.</b>

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.150
He seems pretty off the rails.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.120
Why don't they just go to the metropolitan 
government building, and get it over with?

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.860
Yeah, that made me wonder, too.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.810
Then we can wrap this up, and I 
can go see abandoned train lines!

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:18.640
Huh?

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.780
Um...

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.260
<i>Just target me!</i>

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.150
<i>What moved you to take such dangerous action?</i>

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.210
<i>This is an act of terrorism, 
involving innocent civilians!</i>

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.370
Poor governor...

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.480
First, corruption charges kill 
his popularity, and now this.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.460
Not necessarily.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:34.500
Huh?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.210
He might be thinking he can turn it all 
around, if he plays his cards right.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.130
<b>Perpetrator Identified</b>

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.210
So fast! Nice work, Madoka-chan!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.840
<b>I support the Peace Party's Naganuma-sensei 
Let's restore politics to what they should be!</b>

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.460
The Peace Party...

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:45.950
The opposition candidate, huh?

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.930
Kobari Masataka, age forty, single.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.080
Kobari?

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.810
At the moment, we're just 
gathering supporting evidence.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:00.560
For now, let's contact HQ—

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:01.400
Naganuma-san!

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.710
We hear the person responsible is 
from your group of supporters!

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.660
Didn't you see any warning signs?

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.580
Ah...

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.470
You'll surely be expected 
to assume responsibility.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.220
Please, not right now...

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.370
We have been unable to contact 
him for the past month or so.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.220
We'll hold an official press conference later.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.590
Please! Just one comment!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.580
Governor!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.590
The attacker has publicly stated 
that you are his target.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.760
How do you intend to counter this threat?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.860
Don't worry!

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.100
I have led this prefecture for 
seven and a half years!

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.180
As incompetent as I, Terao Kazuyoshi, may be, 
I refuse to be a burden on my constituents!

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.930
I will protect their peace and safety!

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.530
I find it hard to believe that he 
and Inagi-kun are responsible.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.460
I'm not sure how much longer 
Kuroki-san and his crew can wait!

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.030
Huh?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.080
If we frame it as traffic support for now, 
we won't need permission, right?

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.250
This street is currently blocked from use.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.310
Wait at least, uh...

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.310
One hour until it's cleared!

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:06.920
He's waiting?

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:15.290
Will you really keep your promise?

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:16.930
There's no need for concern.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.150
Go straight to the metropolitan government 
building, no matter what happens.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:32.320
I have no choice!

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:42.750
Oscar VI!

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:43.590
Got it!

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.800
The target's headed to 
Shinjuku via the train tracks!

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.180
He hopes to reach the metropolitan government 
building from the track guardrails.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.430
Let me handle this!

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.390
His biggest mistake was entering the tracks!

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.270
Haruka-chan's unusually fired up.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.710
We have permission.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.480
All Oscar units, return to 
exchange battery packs.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.260
Cut it out, Oscar II!

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:16.100
Oscar II, I, and VI have returned!

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.640
Please let me down!

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.390
Hang on, I'll open the aft hatch.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.340
Roger!

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.990
Thanks! I'll return it later.

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.400
Okay, no problem.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:28.710
President?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.180
Oh, sorry.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.840
Something about that incident's bothering me, 
so I'm borrowing your computer.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.760
Oh, the TV finally gave out?

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:38.970
It was pretty old.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.150
What? He still hasn't been caught?

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:42.920
No.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.980
There's some talk that he was 
against projection mapping.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.260
That reconstruction event?

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:49.160
What are you doing?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.690
Oh, sorry.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.910
<b>Do you wish to patch this program?
Program Name: Liko app</b>

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.910
<i>Would you like to patch the software?</i>

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:56.830
Isn't this the Liko modding tool 
that's distributed underground?

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.540
I borrowed it from a friend.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.500
<b>Installing</b>

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.500
I heard it'd make her even 
more useful than before.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.630
<b>Update complete.</b>

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.630
<i>Liko's updated!</i>

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.740
She's just freeware, anyway,

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.550
and it's your computer, after all. 
I don't see a problem.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:11.590
Thank you.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:15.330
It's just that I haven't found enough 
references for my paper topic.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.230
And you want Liko to help you?

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.310
Yes, it's about the Fruit of Tragedy.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.670
You're writing about that terrorist attack?

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:24.560
Um... It was about a decade ago, right?

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.270
Right. But I haven't found anything 
about the cult leader back then.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.090
Ah...

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.740
Yeah, that might be hard to find.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.700
<b>Operation "Go with the Tracks!"</b>

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:37.940
Will this work?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.960
I support this plan.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.910
It's logical and appropriate.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.750
I'm impressed it was put together so quickly.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.340
<b>Data Transfer in Progress</b>

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.010
Madoka-chan, please request permission.

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.570
How is it there, Kyoukai-san?

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.800
Proceeding with preparations, as requested.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.560
All right! Just wait, perp!

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:58.670
I'm furious that I had to cancel my tour!

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.460
There's more to find?

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:05.180
Just a little something that might help 
when we apprehend the perp.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.690
Permission granted!

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:08.980
Permission granted!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.440
<b>Permission Granted</b>

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:12.440
We have permission from all rail agencies.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:15.030
Okay, now we just need to execute the plan!

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.670
All right! Let's stop this guy!

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:18.280
Oh!

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:23.200
Sorry to interject when you're all ready to go...

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.290
Huh?

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.240
But the governor has not given permission.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.170
Huh? But this doesn't fall under his jurisdiction!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:32.960
<b>Permission Denied</b>

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.750
Well, apparently, the new elevated tracks 
on Shinjuku Station's north side

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.340
belong to the prefecture.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.050
<b>Permission Denied</b>

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.050
Huh?!

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.300
You've got to be kidding.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.670
What's wrong with the governor?

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.960
He's the one being targeted!

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.390
<b>Goal: 0 Crime</b>

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.390
Everyone...

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.350
We are now prepared to apprehend the terrorist!

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:53.890
Is that

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.240
a missile?

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.630
No.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.590
I'd foreseen the rise of 
numerous futuristic crimes,

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:02.220
and asked my alma mater, OIT,

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:06.780
or the Oshamanbe Institute of Technology, 
to develop this using my private funds.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:09.740
It's a non-lethal, criminal-suppression rocket!

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:14.390
It is equipped with a unique anti-phase, 
high-voltage generator,

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:19.810
which enables it to neutralize that 
EM dome with little issue!

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.610
So that's his play...

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:28.000
He interfered with our work 
to regain his approval ratings.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.760
Still, using that won't leave the perp unscathed.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.730
Um, what are you looking at, Haruka-san?

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.670
A diorama of the very first Amarube railway 
bridge, which was part of the San'in Line.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.170
Don't you just love the sturdy steel framework?

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.620
Look at the power and beauty of its form!

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.120
Let's not use this time for personal hobbies.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.550
Do you notice anything?

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.090
Huh?

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:04.100
There's a father with a young daughter

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.810
in all of the dioramas.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:09.020
Yes. This pair is the key

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.480
to cracking this case.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.150
But Kobari is single and has no children.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:17.700
I thought so.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:21.820
That's it!

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.280
Continue the operation! 
We'll get to Shinjuku first!

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:28.230
Funasaka-san, contact the governor!

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.010
What?

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:41.560
The rocket can't be launched? What's going on?

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.720
It's aviation law.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.180
It would violate aviation 
law article 99, section 2.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.280
You won't get away with claiming ignorance.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:55.630
We could, however, proceed with our 
operation without infringing on any laws.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.030
<i>Damn that Unit 8!</i>

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.990
After so much preparation, 
why let Unit 8 take over?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.900
I have determined that doing so

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.660
would better let us safeguard our citizens.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:10.990
But, Governor, aren't you against Willwear use?

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:11.660
Well,

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.830
regardless of my personal opinions, 
civilian lives come first.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.540
That is my civic duty, after all.

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:22.190
I guess politicians have to be 
this shameless to succeed.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.240
Let's go over the operation.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.640
Kyoukai-kun will soon finish

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:31.310
preparing the anti-phase, 
high-voltage generator.

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.990
Once we hook it to the Shinjuku Station rails

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.420
and activate its voltage, the repulsion will 
blow a hole in the target's EM dome.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:40.040
Then we'll rush that point.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.780
That role falls to me, obviously!

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:44.550
No, I can handle close-quarters combat.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.740
Let me go.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.480
Huh?

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:47.680
Haruka-chan?

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.760
No way!

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.310
Haruka-san, you're specialized for 
network and search operations.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.990
Do you all know anything about 
signals and security devices?

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.630
Besides, there's one more important 
reason why I should go.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.980
Is it something to do with the dioramas?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.670
Oh, that'd be two reasons, then!

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:05.930
So can I count on you?

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:06.850
Yes!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.140
Commencing preparation to equip Willwear.

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.430
Vitals, all green.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.100
Lock.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.140
Meti-structure, set Ibuki unit.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.650
Here it comes! The Chiki 5500,

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.220
a cargo train for transporting long rails!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.380
It's finally time to put an end to this.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:52.770
Er... Huh?

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.940
Wow, I've never seen it before!

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:57.030
It really does pack a punch!

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:58.730
Was this the important reason?

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.670
Here comes the enemy.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:09.350
Power on the anti-phase, high-voltage generator!

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.250
Forget it!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:20.330
Switch the third crossover and 
the sixth scissors crossing.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.130
Next, switch the second single cross

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.620
and the seventh scissors crossing.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.730
Infiltrate the fourth switch system,

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:31.220
switch the double slip, DC, and Y-junction.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.350
Going in!

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.980
Just as I expected.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.860
Prepare backup operation!

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:57.330
There's nowhere left to go.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:01.630
Will she really be all right by herself?

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.570
We have to trust her.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:10.550
The original Amarube bridge was the best.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.260
Huh?

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.060
What?

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.720
What is she talking about?

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.430
The way it reaches into 
the sky, without pretense...

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:20.140
And all those bare steel beams get to you.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.800
What are you talking about?

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.950
Building a bridge in such a place is

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.070
like challenging nature itself, don't you think?

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.650
All that passion and expertise in one bridge!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.580
It really tugs on your heartstrings!

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.240
Wait, he's actually listening?

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:39.330
I've never seen the original itself, of course,

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:43.370
but I was able to experience the feeling, 
thanks to a wonderful diorama.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.710
Kobari-san,

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.420
it was your diorama.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.010
He's the one who made it?

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.290
I like trains, buses,

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:59.250
extinguishers, and signals... 
All kinds of things made by people.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:02.570
It's thanks to you, Kobari-san.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:07.660
But why are you trying to run, even if it 
means destroying Shinjuku Station?

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.940
You love trains!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.910
You're a kind man who also loves children.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.480
Kobari-san,

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.640
records state that you're childless.

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:30.340
But you send a fixed monthly sum under a 
different name to a Filipino girl, don't you?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.010
Huh?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:34.660
I'm sorry, but it's my job to look around.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:40.210
I learned the girl won't live long unless she 
gets an organ transplant in America.

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.150
She's your daughter,

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.650
isn't she?

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.240
I'll give you my full support 
for the organ transplant.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.380
But you are not to speak a word of this,

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:58.260
other than about your relationship with 
Naganuma. That is my condition.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:00.880
I have no daughter.

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:03.720
My goal is

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.790
to punish the governor!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.750
That's all!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.670
No, Oscar III!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.630
Get away from him!

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:13.480
Get out!

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:14.680
Please get out!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.680
I won't!

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.400
All right!

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.470
Oscar II!

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.860
Got it!

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.860
Okay, go!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.400
Power on the generator!

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.290
I'm sorry.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.620
Hey, that doesn't look good!

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.750
Oscar III!

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:51.210
Please remember the main Sekihoku Line's...

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:54.420
Shoubou Pass!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:59.700
Remember the powerful DD51 trains 
that raced up the steep slope

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.350
with their twin engines!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:02.970
Isn't that

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.660
just like you and your daughter?

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:08.030
Missing either one would mean failure!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:10.610
You'd be overcome by the slopes of the pass!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:14.900
You have to keep running together, hand-in-hand,

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:18.180
on that long rail known as life!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.180
Please don't commit any more crimes.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.330
Don't sever the link that holds 
the two engines together!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.350
I want to help both you and your daughter.

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:31.790
That's why you need to tell us the whole truth

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:33.670
by turning yourself in!

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:47.880
He stopped.

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:51.440
I...

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:52.860
I just...

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.860
You are not to speak a word.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.410
Kobari-san...

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:05.600
And here I thought you'd chosen 
your daughter over your hobby,

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:06.930
you loser.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:09.620
Bye, Kobari-san.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.300
Oh, no! I've lost control of the system!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:15.880
What?

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:16.550
Huh?

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.720
At a time like this?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:19.750
This is bad!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.720
The Wear can't withstand this amount of output.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:22.760
Oscar III!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.440
Kobari-san?

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.490
I have no daughter...

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:47.370
I have no daughter!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:48.590
Kobari-san...

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.250
Kobari-san!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.550
Oh, no...

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:03.760
Who gave him

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:07.350
Logos's Willwear without permission?

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:13.710
<i>Some have voiced approval of the governor's 
response to the most recent incident.</i>

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:17.490
<i>The governor's supporters are hopeful 
about the upcoming elections...</i>

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:16.290
Funasaka-san.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.630
About Kobari's Willwear...

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:21.240
A program enabling external control

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.920
was snuck into its system.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:27.050
Do you think you can trace it to the mastermind?

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.000
It will be difficult.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:33.020
I wish my council had 
investigative authority, as well.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:37.010
I hear you.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:40.260
<i>As previously reported, 
Diet member Naganuma Daizou,</i>

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:45.840
<b>Saint IMS Hospital</b>

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:44.480
<i>of the Peace Party, who was planning to 
enter the upcoming gubernatorial race,</i>

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:48.080
<i>was found dead today, at 4:20 PM, in his room</i>

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:50.250
<i>at the Akasaka Diet dormitory.</i>

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.060
<i>The cause of death was acute cardiac arrest.</i>

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.360
<i>Some sources report it was a suicide,</i>

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:59.730
<i>but no link between him and the attack 
on the governor has been established.</i>

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:02.400
Why would he commit suicide?

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:06.680
He'd turned down Kobari's request for help.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:11.310
He'd received reports that their intermediary 
was operating an illegal organization.

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:13.400
But he felt responsible,

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:17.050
feeling that the decision 
had made Kobari reckless.

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:19.270
In the end, only the governor

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:21.290
gained anything from this.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:23.880
I don't understand.

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:28.260
There are all these dots around 
this case that I can't connect.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.980
I can't quite put a finger on it,

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:33.230
but I think there's a reason...

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.120
Several reasons, even.

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:37.930
Someone who was involved

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:39.980
is still hiding?

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.060
Haruka-san?

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.860
I couldn't do anything...

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:53.540
That's not true!

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:57.380
You gathered donations for 
Kobari-san's daughter's surgery.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:00.750
But now, Kobari-san's wish

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:03.170
will never come true.

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:09.220
Sorry.

00:22:10.490 --> 00:22:12.100
Let me stay like this a while.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:51.950
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:53.670
In the next episode— Whoa, new Willwear!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:24:04.950
File 8: Ulti-maid-ronde

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:54.910
Whose? Madoka-san's?

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:57.360
Or is it Kyoukai-san's, of all people? 
Or maybe even Hinata-chan?

00:23:57.360 --> 00:23:59.030
Or even... Could it be Shinmei Amu-chan?

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:00.740
Whose transformation scene
would you like to see?

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.300
Next time, "Ulti-maid-ronde."

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:04.790
The answer to the question will 
arrive in 604,800 seconds!
